WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.295
TEZAUR is a thesis assistant that works only from your own library. Here are three studies, as plain text files.

00:00:12.394 --> 00:00:19.974
The ingest command indexes them locally, together with the BibTeX bibliography. Nothing leaves the computer.

00:00:23.605 --> 00:00:29.484
The sources command lists the indexed documents, each tied to its bibliography entry.

00:00:33.398 --> 00:00:41.423
Search returns the matching passages and shows how many query terms each one covers. It needs no language model.

00:00:44.466 --> 00:00:51.192
Here is a draft excerpt with citations. Some claims are faithful to the sources, others are not.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:01:05.069
The audit command checks every citation against its source. An overreaching claim is marked unsupported, and a missing key is flagged. It is a mechanical check, not proof.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:18.748
The refs command finds cited keys that appear nowhere. For generated answers TEZAUR needs a local model, which is not shown here.
